        "url": "https://www.stocktitan.net/news/JYNT/the-joint-corp-reports-first-quarter-2026-financial-en8db5qckrn9.html",
        "snippet": "The Joint Q1 Revenue Rises 13%, Reaffirms 2026 Outlook | JYNT Stock News\n\n# The Joint Corp. Reports First Quarter 2026 Financial Results\n\nRhea-AI Impact\n\n(High)\n\nRhea-AI Sentiment\n\n(Neutral)\n\nTags\n\n## Rhea-AI Summary\n\n- English\n- Arabic\n- French\n- German\n- Italian\n- Korean\n- Spanish\n\nThe Joint Corp. (NASDAQ: JYNT) reported Q1 2026 results: revenue $14.8M (+13% YoY), consolidated net income $1.3M (+34% YoY), and adjusted EBITDA $3.5M (+22% YoY). System-wide sales were $126.1M (down 4.9%) and comp sales were -4.2%. Company repurchased 137,000 shares for $1.1M and continued refranchising, signing a $2.3M sale for 45 clinics in Southern California.\n\nUnrestricted cash was $20.7M; company reiterated 2026 guidance for system-wide sales of $519M–$552M and consolidated adjusted EBITDA $12.5M–$13.5M.\n\nLoading translation...\n\nAI-generated analysis. Not financial advice.\n\n### Positive\n\n- Revenue +13% YoY to $14.8M\n- Net income +34% YoY to $1.3M\n- Adjusted EBITDA +22% YoY to $3.5M\n- Repurchased $1.",
